    "body": "## What\n\nImport upstream [PR #13285](https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/pull/13285), preserving both commits, @affaffaff's authorship, and changelog attribution. The implementation is unchanged. Also route the existing lint/type checks to the repo-restricted ARM runner with its data-disk Bun cache: the first pipeline exhausted the OS disk shared with Forgejo. This does not merge the separate ARM-CI overhaul in PR #2.\n\nThe contributor's original explanation: \"Ctrl+Up or Ctrl+Down opens transcript scroll mode with the editor and status line pinned below. each press jumps to the previous or next prompt.\"\n\n## Why\n\nThe fork owner requested: \"lets take the not-yet-merged upstream PR onto our omp fork for now\" for \"navigating between my input messages/turns\", rather than fixed-row paging. Related: https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi/issues/8726.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `bun test packages/tui/test/transcript-scroll.test.ts packages/tui/test/terminal-selection-color.test.ts`: 11 passed, 0 failed, 47 assertions.\n- Source CLI in a real tmux PTY: three user prompts separated by 45-line replies; Ctrl+Up selected user 3 then user 2, and Ctrl+Down returned to user 3. Editor/status stayed pinned. Typing returned to the draft; reopening and Escape preserved it. Saved messages stayed unchanged, with no additional session entries.\n- Reused an installed native addon and existing HTML export asset; no local native/CLI compilation. Live-model streaming and mouse selection were not manually exercised; automated tests cover selection and overlay yielding.\n- Strict Woodpecker config lint: valid, 0 errors/warnings. [PR pipeline #21](https://ci.n3t.work/repos/3/pipeline/21) passed lint and all workspace type checks for head `4e04e7d3a7`. Full `bun check` was not run: this pipeline checks TS, not Rust.\n- Merged without squash as `ac649352d9`; feature branch retained. [Arch pipeline #83](https://ci.n3t.work/repos/2/pipeline/83) automatically started for that exact merge commit.\n- Retained upstream changelog entry, PR link, and author credit.\n\n---\n\n- [ ] `bun check` passes\n- [x] Tested locally\n- [x] CHANGELOG updated with the required attribution (if user-facing; internal issue fixes use issue links, external contributions add the PR link and contributor credit after creation)",
    "changed_files": 12,
